0 0 0 0 7 7 0 0\n0 0 0 0 0 0 7 7 0 0\n0 3 0 0 0 0 3 0 0 0\n0 0 3 0 0 3 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 3 0 0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 3 3 0 0 0 0 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Initialize output grid with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        # Dictionary to store min and max column for each value\n        bounds = {}\n        \n        # Find min and max column for each non-zero value in the row\n        for j in range(cols):\n            val = grid[i][j]\n            if val != 0:\n                if val in bounds:\n                    min_col, max_col = bounds[val]\n                    bounds[val] = (min(min_col, j), max(max_col, j))\n                else:\n                    bounds[val] = (j, j)\n        \n        # Fill the ranges in the output\n        for val, (min_col, max_col) in bounds.items():\n            for j in range(min_col, max_col + 1):\n                output[i][j] = val\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    \n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Initialize output grid with zeros\n    output = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    for i in range(rows):\n        # Dictionary to store min and max column for each value\n        bounds = {}\n        \n        # Find min and max column for each non-zero value in the row\n        for j in range(cols):\n            val = grid[i][j]\n            if val != 0:\n                if val in bounds:\n                    min_col, max_col = bounds[val]\n                    bounds[val] = (min(min_col, j), max(max_col, j))\n                else:\n                    bounds[val] = (j, j)\n        \n        # Fill the ranges in the output\n        for val, (min_col, max_col) in bounds.items():\n            for j in range(min_col, max_col + 1):\n                output[i][j] = val\n    \n    return output",
